Title: AROS: entropy seed and memory for machine code
Repository: luajit
Base: 96f7b297326e9fd454b7186c6858b2773f94a0dc
Requires: nothing
Date: 2026-11-20
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: LuaJIT builds for an unknown system (TARGET_SYS=Other) stop at "Missing secure PRNG seed for this OS" and "Missing OS support for explicit placement of executable memory": AROS has no /dev/urandom and no mmap.
Change: The PRNG seed comes from entropy.resource directly (not getentropy(): see lj_aros.c). Machine code memory comes from exec.library in the new lj_aros.c: AllocMem(MEMF_EXECUTABLE), without LuaJIT's address hints (AllocAbs() with those addresses stopped mainline in tlsf_allocabs); protection changes are no-ops. The exec calls live in their own file because the AROS headers and LuaJIT both define a type named Node.
Scope: AROS x86_64 (mainline tested); no effect elsewhere
Upstream: local-only
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110) with no implicit function declarations; in LÖVE 12.0 on pool v1-3 (exec 51.17), 2026-11-20: jit.status() true, a trace compiled on the main thread (a 5e7-iteration loop 0.94 s against 4.29 s with jit.off()), ffi structs, arrays and pointers, clean exit
Removal: None planned.
